```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // requires len(text) <= 100000 is a precondition the host guarantees,
        // so the text is forwarded unchanged.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true and present(session_id). The output type has
        // no error case, so a confirmation that fails either clause must not be
        // returned. Trap instead.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("ResponseChannel did not confirm delivery");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("ResponseChannel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. Adding a file write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or an HTTP fetch to `metadata.internal.example` would need capabilities this node does not hold, and it would also require imports the `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target does not provide. Logging and enrichment should be done by a node that is granted those capabilities, or by the host.

